infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title any vs unknown — the escape hatch vs the safe top type
  desc Both can hold any value; only one keeps the downstream chain checked
  compares
    - label any
      children
        - label Zero friction up front
          desc Access any property, call, or index immediately — no proof required
        - label Checking disabled
          desc Assignable both to and from everything, so it slips into typed slots
        - label Contagious
          desc Every access off an any yields any — the hole spreads down the chain
        - label Bill deferred and compounding
          desc A runtime crash plus every silently-poisoned call site downstream
    - label unknown
      children
        - label One narrow at the boundary
          desc A few lines — typeof, in, a guard, or Zod — parsed once
        - label Must prove the shape
          desc Nothing usable until you narrow it to something specific
        - label Downstream stays checked
          desc The whole chain past the boundary keeps full type safety
        - label Correct for untrusted input
          desc JSON.parse, fetch().json(), localStorage, catch vars since TS 4.4
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
